{title: There Is Power in the Blood}
{artist: Lewis E. Jones}
{genre: Gospel}
{flow: Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: G}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Would you be [G]free from the burden of sin?
There's [D7]power in the blood, power in the [G]blood
Would you o'er [G]evil a victory win?
There's [D7]wonderful power in the [G]blood
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
There is [G]power, power, wonder-working [C]power
In the [G]blood of the [D7]Lamb
There is [G]power, power, wonder-working [C]power
In the [G]precious blood of the [D7]Lamb[G]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Would you be [G]free from your passion and pride?
There's [D7]power in the blood, power in the [G]blood
Come for a [G]cleansing to Calvary's tide
There's [D7]wonderful power in the [G]blood
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Would you be [G]whiter, much whiter than snow?
There's [D7]power in the blood, power in the [G]blood
Sin-stains are [G]lost in its life-giving flow
There's [D7]wonderful power in the [G]blood
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
